caa817cd7ac99b6f570da0beed72be1424109c694","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1993e4f2cbd0716e2a4f19f295f7407596595bbcf5fd957d2f51847b0d2d55fd"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T09:04:00.679Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T09:04:00.679Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-07T09:04:00.674Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation evidence (branch feat/extension-authoring-contracts, 2026-11-07).\n\nRoot cause: the definition-driven extension option grammar lived in src/cli and ran only on CLI argv dispatch. The SDK path (dispatchActiveExtensionAction in src/sdk/runtime.ts, reached by PmClient.run and MCP) and runRegisteredCommandForTest passed options through raw, so a CLI spelling such as status-filter never reached the handler key statusFilter and the declared default applied instead.\n\nChange:\n- Moved the module to src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts so the SDK can share it (no sdk -> cli import exists anywhere).\n- New normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions folds each declared spelling (statusFilter, status-filter, --status-filter, short letter) into the handler key, treats undefined as omitted, refuses two spellings with different values (extension_option_spelling_conflict, exit 2, names both keys and the handler key), then runs the same coerceLooseCommandOptionsWithFlagDefinitions as CLI dispatch (defaults, coercion, strict validation). Undeclared keys pass through unchanged for SDK compatibility.\n- PmClient.run/MCP dispatch and the harness both call it; the harness finds the declared flags through a WeakMap keyed by activation.commands, so existing package tests need no new argument. A hand-built registry passes options through verbatim.\n- pm contracts --command <cmd> --flags-only --json publishes sdk_option and owner extension on every extension row; help --json options carry the same fields.\n- MCP tool-schema property names now use the same handler key (only changes legacy underscore flags such as --include_history, whose old property includehistory never reached the handler).\n- collectExtensionFlagDefinitionsForCommand moved beside it and is shared by CLI and SDK.\n\nBehavior change for direct callers (migration line): PmClient.run, MCP and the test harness now apply declared defaults and value coercion for extension flags exactly as the CLI does, so a handler that echoes options sees the default keys and booleans instead of raw strings.\n\nVerified: tests/integration/extensions/extension-option-contract.integration.spec.ts (CLI argv, PmClient.run with three spellings, harness, conflict refusal) and tests/unit/sdk/extension-command-options.spec.ts pass. Negative control: replacing the SDK normalizer with identity makes the integration spec fail with selection undefined instead of closed.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"7b0ff75a13327954a8764fecaa817cd7ac99b6f570da0beed72be1424109c694","after_hash":"f3c9d042db9ca4b47a40a73d4071a6b61527949ae257290b424b20d690429ddd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1e82cdb0eec3fb53fcd50095ec6340b046104d1b3a33a18dab4c47b8da9e0e80"}
