{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T10:00:01.499Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T10:00:01.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh, local, uncommitted diff) found four defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- P1: a strict boolean switch passed directly (PmClient.run, MCP or the harness) as \"nonsense\" became true, because the CLI coercer treats a separated token after a switch as a positional. Direct values are now recorded as attached occurrences (like --commit=value), so the existing attached-switch check refuses them with extension_flag_value_invalid; arrays become one occurrence per entry. Regression in tests/unit/sdk/extension/command-options.spec.ts; negative control (passing the folded options without recorded occurrences) fails it.\n- P2: the root-only refusal ran only for commands that declare flags. It moved into refuseUndeclaredRootOnlyOptions, called from the extension action wrapper for every extension command; the integration spec now covers demo-plain (no flags) with --all and --explain (code unknown_option).\n- P2: the signature gate skipped callable variable exports (runUpdateMany, resolveContentFieldFilters). It now checks every exported function and every exported variable annotation (checked_values in the snapshot); eight more gaps closed (UpdateManyCommandOptions, UpdateManyResult, ContentFieldFilters, MissingMetadataFilters, BuiltinItemType, GovernanceStartBlockerEnforcement).\n- P2: inline import(\"./x.js\").T references bypassed the visitor. ImportTypeNode qualifiers now resolve like ordinary references; typeof import(...) names no type.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T10:00:01.499Z"}],"before_hash":"f5568bf046d2c00fe243ffb92d86495bd1c49ccf69073791147be86f520b0c51","after_hash":"ca840e6cd9f7aad9f2b2aa95e697661542fd2f50ea5cb30671f6df10db20336b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5f450a05f804eb67fb9977b80c23ac485251196e3e2f0fb1438f1285287461f4"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T10:13:06.744Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T10:13:06.743Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) confirmed the round 1 fixes and found four more defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- P1: the root-only refusal also ran on core commands that an extension only augments with flags (pm-command-kit adds flags to list, so pm list --all failed with unknown_option). It now runs only for extension-created command nodes (isExtensionCreatedCommand); the integration spec registers a flag on list and asserts pm list --all --demo-extra keeps status all.\n- P2: nested list values passed directly ([[true, \"false\"]]) were validated as scalars before flattening. Direct occurrences now flatten recursively, matching the list coercer.\n- P2 (gate): typeof HiddenClass (a TypeQuery) bypassed the census. Type queries now resolve; a query of a package value (typeof internalRun) follows that value's own signature, with a cycle guard. Following it exposed two real gaps (PmSettings for sdk/merge resolveProjectMergeTypeFolders, LoadedRuntimeSchemaSections for loadGuardedRuntimeSchema), now re-exported.\n- P2 (gate): enum member references (State.Ready) now resolve to the declaring enum.\nTest seams: following type queries also reached the _testOnly* exports (internal functions exposed for pm's own tests). These are exempt by naming convention and counted as exempt_test_seams per entrypoint in the snapshot, so publishing internal test-seam types never becomes a requirement.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T10:13:06.744Z"}],"before_hash":"ca840e6cd9f7aad9f2b2aa95e697661542fd2f50ea5cb30671f6df10db20336b","after_hash":"20d1f2a493c62abc3f439fd762fb99f13b521449ad138db92f2d931833a368ea","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"085b83bd386274b95f27b03359d60c2300af6b2bf86d0d096ea58545ff52f923"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T10:28:22.424Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T10:28:22.424Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) found three P2 defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- Direct short aliases were folded case-insensitively, so with --small/-s and --sort-order/-S a direct { S } reached small and { s, S } raised a false spelling conflict. Short letters are now indexed case-sensitively (Commander keeps -s and -S distinct on the CLI); long spellings still fold through the camel-case key.\n- On a core command an extension augments (provider mixed, for example an extension flag on list), extension rows carried no owner or sdk_option. Extension-contributed rows are now decorated on every command; inherited_flags stays limited to extension-provided commands. The integration spec asserts the mixed list entry.\n- The signature gate ignored type queries of methods and callable properties (typeof api.run). publicSignatureNodes now covers every function-like declaration and property annotations; the real SDK has no new gaps.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T10:28:22.424Z"}],"before_hash":"20d1f2a493c62abc3f439fd762fb99f13b521449ad138db92f2d931833a368ea","after_hash":"c02a09d26eef44e0841d027e1361287b2d8a733641e53ec524e19c8d474afe78","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"913dcd4a064964a1ac1bbfa413b5fa82177df016849785e5de604727786b0c92"}
