{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T11:10:21.284Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The integration spec drives one command through CLI argv, PmClient.run with three spellings and the harness and gets the same selection; conflicting spellings exit 2 with extension_option_spelling_conflict; contracts list sdk_option and owner; negative control (identity normalizer) fails the spec with selection undefined"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A CLI-spelled extension option passed to PmClient.run or the harness reaches the handler key exactly as on the CLI, conflicting spellings are refused, and contracts publish the key"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T11:10:21.284Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-07T11:10:21.252Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-07T11:10:21.252Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"One definition-driven normalizer in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts (moved from src/cli) now serves CLI argv dispatch, PmClient.run, MCP and runRegisteredCommandForTest. normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions folds each declared spelling (statusFilter, status-filter, --status-filter, a case-sensitive short letter) into the handler key, records direct values as attached occurrences so strict booleans are validated without the CLI positional fallback, refuses two spellings with different values with extension_option_spelling_conflict, then applies the shared defaults and coercion. pm contracts and help --json publish owner extension and sdk_option on every extension flag row, including extension rows on core commands. The shared coercer no longer lets a lower-cased short alias absorb another flag's own key. MCP tool-schema property names use the handler key. The normalizer and its definition type are exported from sdk/authoring and the aggregate. Migration: direct callers now receive declared defaults and coerced values, as CLI callers always did."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Direct callers reach extension handlers under the same option keys, defaults and coercion as the CLI"}],"before_hash":"8031614d2f49be759ac67845cea81bd56c58e6e205df1474dd518fc13a53ad42","after_hash":"718b43cfd653720cd30c460ca9e69c334ad6023aff2bbc5aa7b25f9d6d598c4d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:10:21.252Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"37ecfa44bf38fa4aaaa74a4558161b461e28c8491f2cf271d9ea40b125aafbbb"}
